From 514b3a2c52e83aea6012f246351cf2e671f03855 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 12:22:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shell): unify app shell nav, routing recovery &
 deep-links

Implements the Wave 1 multi-surface UX audit (#104):

- deepLinks: canonicalize /stats AND /statistics straight to /history in
  one hop (no /stats -> /statistics -> /history double redirect).
- Unify active-tab detection across header, mobile sheet and bottom nav
  via a shared logical `tab` id, and paint every active surface with the
  same solid action token (was action-soft on the bottom nav only).
- Account bottom-nav cell is now a single control: a labelled navigation
  button to /profile. Removed the invisible overlaid Clerk UserButton
  (the double control confused screen readers and dead-mapped the tap).
- Replace the full branded splash route fallback with a lightweight
  inline skeleton; the nav shell already lives outside the boundary so
  chunk loads no longer flash the splash.
- Brand button: add aria-label "Score Easy home" and hide the SCORE/EASY
  wordmark (and its <br/>) from the accessible name.
- Sport-scoped 404s now offer a guaranteed Home escape.
- Legacy /game/:id resume links resolve against saved on-device drafts
  (tennis quick + cricket Test) and redirect to the canonical scorer URL,
  falling back to the recovery screen when no live draft exists.

Deferred (noted in PR): sets/goals quick-match per-matchId deep-link
URL, which would require refactoring MonoQuickMatch + both scorer
components (out of the issue's named files). Those quick matches remain
resumable at /:sport/quick via their existing per-sport draft.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
